# 15. Cross-Agency Comparison

The current evidence suggests that the agencies differ in where their performance systems are strongest.

| Dimension                         | BLM        | Forest Service       | NPS                         | NWRS                        |
| --------------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Standardized condition monitoring | Strong     | Moderate/strong      | Strong                      | Variable                    |
| Long-term ecological monitoring   | Strong     | Strong               | Very strong                 | Variable                    |
| Landscape-scale assessment        | Increasing | Strong potential     | Moderate                    | Important                   |
| Explicit ecological standards     | Strong     | Variable by resource | Strong preservation mandate | Strong conservation mandate |
| Multiple-use tradeoff complexity  | Very high  | Very high            | Moderate                    | Moderate                    |
| Direct wildlife emphasis          | Moderate   | Moderate             | High                        | Very high                   |
| External ecological pressures     | Very high  | Very high            | High                        | Very high                   |
| Attribution difficulty            | High       | Very high            | High                        | High                        |

These are **research characterizations, not performance rankings**.

They identify where subsequent evidence collection should concentrate.

